1.What is Emmit?
a. Emmit is a toolkit for developers.It uses abbreviations and shorthand expressions to quickly generate full piece of code.While emit is enabled by default for HTML and CSS files in VScode. It requires small configuration to work with React’s JSX Syntax. By adding specific settings to your settings.json file in vs code to Emmit to recognize .jsx files.
2. Difference between Library and Framework?
a. Framework: Aframework provides a structured environment ,set of tools,guildelimess and often pre-built components to facilitate the applivation development.It defines the overall architecture and flow of the application called by the framework itself.
    Library : A Library is a pre-written code designed to perform specific tasks.Your Application     calls the library functions when ever it needed.
3.What is CDN.Why we use it?
a. CDN (Content Delivery Network) is a network of servers worldwide that stores copies of files.Instead of downloading React, we use <script src="cdn-link"> to load it directly in browser.
      We use CDN for:
	Faster loading from nearest server
	No installation needed
	Always get latest version
	Reduce our server load

